on" or "crisis" news might trigger a sell after the market has already bottomed out.\n*   **Rapid Reversals:** In volatile periods like COVID, sentiment can shift dramatically day-to-day. A "positive outlook" one day might be negated by "second wave" fears the next, causing whipsaws if the strategy enters based on the initial sentiment.\n*   **Nuance Misses:** While negation is included, complex news articles can have multiple conflicting sentiments or subtle implications that a keyword-based system might miss, leading to misinterpretations. For example, "lack of recession fears" might be interpreted as a positive, but if the market is already in a downturn, it might be a temporary relief rally.	N/A	[0.021839218,0.03886792,-0.047812145,-0.019870004,-0.012820462,0.04100817,-0.029805392,-0.0075887865,0.028939003,-0.10219313,-0.014481047,0.057434402,0.01196531,-0.005423647,-0.008142131,-0.01653987,0.026565408,-0.07194893,0.015423392,0.006838956,-0.004233674,0.021692177,0.0132044675,0.03020881,0.033031516,0.015423652,0.022422671,-0.012729602,0.0011020572,0.22531569,-0.0016609052,-0.062156994,-0.0069409874,0.021690026,-0.015329059,0.022341978,0.03363056,-0.011012686,0.0022779407,0.0063239527,0.019763434,0.03131489,0.04023133,0.049246922,0.04583424,-0.03148458,-0.0017943867,0.02134045,0.0050495644,0.0059501743,-0.027548227,-0.024962736,0.018757097,-0.031921122,-0.004561161,0.03998918,0.019162802,0.008022099,0.02347656,-0.0039577545,-0.038840033,0.03629336,0.0819987,-0.020512793,0.057874583,-0.012642579,0.004088528,0.025769526,0.021221163,-0.040744327,-0.0016662724,-0.004826006,-0.02567534,-0.0031438826,-0.037242763,-0.028716253,-0.026830245,0.019834947,-0.028123662,0.041891098,-0.0077667865,-0.029850168,-0.030986955,0.041283898,0.012454852,0.08468536,0.016293313,-0.021982066,0.008254207,-0.014686569,0.02304719,-0.00030574255,0.031523697,-0.0020727515,-0.009658336,0.0058302507,-0.015113556,0.005482243,-0.019278673,0.036345173,-0.056625362,-0.0024554185,0.027798265,-0.01659