y_score += 1.0 # Contrarian signal: market is oversold, potential bounce\n\n    # --- 5. Final Decision ---\n    # A BUY signal requires a score surpassing the threshold AND the trend not being bearish.\n    if buy_score >= DECISION_THRESHOLD and macd_line > signal_line:\n        return "BUY"\n    \n    # A SELL signal requires a score surpassing the threshold AND the trend not being bullish.\n    elif sell_score >= DECISION_THRESHOLD and macd_line < signal_line:\n        return "SELL"\n        \n    # Default to HOLD, reducing noise and preventing low-conviction trades.\n    return "HOLD"	f76ee72c6472dcffda842116a77c9f6ce2b79fec058bb5fa2d0b3d13d2ee3909	This self-improvement enhances the parent strategy by replacing the lagging EMA crossover with a more responsive MACD indicator for superior trend analysis. The core logic is evolved from a rigid boolean (`AND`) system to a flexible weighted scoring model. This model aggregates signals from trend (MACD), momentum (RSI), and sentiment, requiring stronger conviction to issue a trade. This change, combined with the retained volatility regime switch, is designed to reduce false signals in choppy markets and improve overall robustness, directly addressing lessons on avoiding whipsaws and sentiment traps.	bba3c7cc-fd9f-4a93-ab43-34a1a96b154b	2026-06-01 18:56:05.344498-04
