 self-improvement enhances the parent strategy's robustness by introducing a multi-layered trend confirmation and more explicit exit logic. A new 50-period slow EMA acts as a long-term regime filter. The core logic is restructured to first check for clear exit signals (e.g., EMA cross-under, mean-reversion target hit) before evaluating new entries. Buy signals in trending markets now require a strict "EMA cascade" (Price > 12 > 26 > 50 EMA) for higher conviction, reducing false signals during consolidations. Sentiment keywords are updated with more contemporary and nuanced economic terms.	1d01fbfa-171e-4cc2-9721-185a8939a2d6	2026-06-01 21:03:13.606775-04
